inline_comments.comment:
The `[\s]+` rule (SPACELIST) matches all whitespace including newline characters (`\n`). Because it appears before the `[\n]+` rule (NL) on line 12, jison will always prefer SPACELIST when it sees a newline — making the `NL` token unreachable. As a result, the `eol: NL` production in the grammar can never fire; only `eol: EOF` is reachable. This means there is no way to parse line endings as logical separators. The lexer rules for whitespace and newlines need to be restructured so that newlines produce `NL` and spaces/tabs produce a separate `SPACELIST`-equivalent token. For example:
```
[\n]+       return "NL";
[^\S\n]+   return "SPACELIST";
```
